{% comment %}
  Resolves a per-PDP display label for an option variant.

  Option variants are frequently shared across product lines (e.g. the Aluminum
  Pulley Upgrade variant FF-DCC-TV-APU is referenced by both the Telluride/Vail
  and Tahoe cable-crossover PDPs). Its variant title therefore names the line it
  was created for, which reads incorrectly on the sibling PDPs.

  The `variant_label_overrides` field on the (per-product) product_option
  metaobject lets us relabel a referenced variant for that PDP only. The variant,
  its SKU and its price are never touched, so the underlying purchase is
  unchanged.

  Format: one override per line, `VariantID=Label`
    52770268479804=Tahoe / FFT-DCC

  "No Thanks" is not just a label - product-custom-options.js matches
  data-field-name against that exact string to identify the opt-out choice, clear
  the other selections in the group and hide dependent options. So overrides are
  refused in both directions for that sentinel: a "No Thanks" variant keeps its
  title, and an override may not introduce the text. Relabelling the opt-out is a
  deliberate JS change, not a data entry.

  Parameters:
    - product_option: the product_option metaobject holding the overrides
    - variant: the variant being rendered

  Outputs the override label, or nothing when there is no match. Use as:
    {%- capture label_override -%}
      {%- render 'option-variant-label-override', product_option: product_option, variant: variant -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign overrides = product_option.variant_label_overrides
  if overrides != blank and variant.title != 'No Thanks'
    assign variant_id_string = variant.id | append: ''
    assign override_lines = overrides | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
    for override_line in override_lines
      assign override_line = override_line | strip
      assign override_parts = override_line | split: '='
      if override_parts.size < 2
        continue
      endif
      assign override_id = override_parts[0] | strip
      if override_id == variant_id_string
        assign override_label = override_line | remove_first: override_parts[0] | remove_first: '=' | strip
        unless override_label == 'No Thanks'
          echo override_label
        endunless
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
